The Sea Travel Desk is part of the Group COO Office and is responsible for the group-wide international travel policy and process.
  - Design, maintain, and ensure compliance with the Sea International Travel Policy, while continuously identifying opportunities to simplify policy application through system design, workflow optimization, and automation;
  - Processing requests for hotel and flight bookings in a timely and pragmatic manner in accordance with the Sea International Travel Policy;
  - Explore and support the adoption of AI-driven solutions (e.g. intelligent request routing, data validation, anomaly detection, reporting automation) to improve operational efficiency and user experience;
  - Working closely with third-party vendors and booking agents to operationalize bookings;
  - Maintaining good and proper records of all travel requests and bookings for billing and management reporting purposes through the self-developed travel management system and purchasing system;
  - Serve as a key point of contact for travelers by resolving inquiries efficiently and improving clarity through better processes and tools;
  - Responding to after-hours travel emergencies and urgent requests;
  - Implement continuous improvement initiatives across travel policy refinement, operational processes, system enhancements, and vendor management, including participation in third-party contract negotiations;
  - Regular reporting to management on travel demand and patterns, as well as ad-hoc analysis when required; and
  - Support special projects related to company travel operations, digital transformation, AI enablement, and cross-functional operational improvements.
  - Bachelor’s Degree in IT or Business field
  - Adaptability to evolving business requirements
  - Willingness to learn and perform tasks across the front, middle and back office
  - Process-driven with strong execution ability
  - Systematic, with excellent attention to details
  - Excellent team player, with willingness to go the extra mile for teammates
  - Proactive in proposing areas for continuous improvement
  - Willingness to adopt AI/use AI as an enabler in his/her daily work
  - Work one weekend every 2 months (compensated with off-in-lieu)

